{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "2c08dee1-45df-80e6-8232-ebf5ec18df66",
  "created_at": "2026-02-25T12:49:52-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Isabel Cabral",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Kevin Sousa",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T12:47:08-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works, this is Kevin."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T12:47:11-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hello. Good afternoon. My name is Isabel Cabral. I am calling about the water. Excuse me, I have written it down, so I say it right."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T12:47:20-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No problem at all, take your time. Go ahead."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T12:47:24-05:00",
      "duration": 18,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you. I live at 201 Chapel Street, in the Historic Hill. After the nor'easter last weekend, Saturday into Sunday, the water comes again into my yard. It runs down the hill from the next street and goes straight into my yard. It is not the first time. Every big rain, the same thing."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T12:47:42-05:00",
      "duration": 11,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, 201 Chapel. Water coming downhill from the street above, into your yard. Got it. Is it a drain on the street that's backed up, or is it just running off the road?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T12:47:53-05:00",
      "duration": 15,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I think it runs off the road, because the drain at the corner, it is full of leaves and does not take the water. I wrote here, the water goes past it. Nobody comes to clean. I am tired of this, I call and nothing changes."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T12:48:08-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, I hear you. That's a fair thing to be fed up about. I'm noting the corner drain is clogged with leaves and the runoff is going into your yard."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T12:48:18-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes. And also, I want to ask. Is it a city drain or a state one? Because someone told me maybe it is the state."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T12:48:27-05:00",
      "duration": 19,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Good question. Most of the drains on the city streets are ours, but some of the bigger roads belong to the state. Chapel's a city street as far as I know, so I'll put it in as ours and have the crew look at it. If it turns out to be the state's, we'd pass it along to them."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T12:48:46-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. That is good. Because there is also my neighbor. She is older, very old, and she cannot get out of her house when the water is high. I worry she is stuck there. [pause] Sorry, I lose my place in the paper."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T12:49:00-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You're fine. So, an elderly neighbor who can't get out when it floods. I'll put that in the notes so they know it's more urgent."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T12:49:09-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Thank you. You know, I stay home a lot now, with the water and everything. I started a puzzle book, to keep my mind sharp. So I have time to watch the water, you see."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T12:49:21-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Well, that's one way to keep an eye on it. Do you want a call back when the crew's been out? What's the best number?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T12:49:30-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yes, please. It is 401-555-0160."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T12:49:32-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Four-oh-one, five-five-five, oh-one-six-oh. Got it. I'm sending this over to the drain crew today, Isabel. They're backed up after the storm, so it may be a few days, but it's in the queue with the neighbor noted."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T12:49:44-05:00",
      "duration": 5,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay. I hope they come. Thank you very much for listening, Kevin."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-02-25T12:49:49-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You bet. Take care, and stay dry."
    }
  ],
